**West of Mauritius** is a guide to one stretch of coast. It runs from Flic en Flac in the north to Le Morne in the south and climbs up into the hills of Chamarel. In French it goes by **Ouest Maurice**.

## What you will find here

- **Areas:** what each village feels like and how to get there.
- **Places:** beaches and viewpoints and walks with a map for each one.
- **Guides:** longer reads on the beaches and the sunsets and everything practical.
- **Living in the West:** where to live and what it costs and how buying a home works.

## Who writes it

West of Mauritius is written by Olivier. He is Mauritian and this guide is his. [Meet Olivier](/en/about/olivier).

## How it is made

Every page is written to be useful on the day you read it. If something changes we update it and you can always see when that happened. Prices and opening hours move fast so we point you to the place itself whenever that matters. You will never find a made up review here.

The photos come from photographers who share their work freely. You can see who took each one on the [photo credits](/en/credits) page.

## Featured places and partner links

Now and then a place may be **featured**. It then shows up first in lists with a small "Featured" label. Some booking links are **partner links** and may earn us a small commission. Both are always marked and neither changes what we say about a place.

## Living in the West

Tell us about your plans through the enquiry form and we will put you in touch with developers and agents on the west coast if you agree to it. Our [privacy policy](/en/privacy) explains how your details are used.

## Say hello

Spotted something out of date? Know a place we should see? Write to us through the [contact page](/en/contact). Every message gets read.
